culate base premium for a potion: 40 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a single rune (component): 25 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a single moonstone (component): 25 G\");\n\n  // === Building block of 3 alike components ===\n  it.todo(\"should charge 50 G base premium for 2 runes (no block)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 60 G base premium for 3 runes (block applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 100 G base premium for 4 runes (no block, block requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 175 G base premium for 7 runes (no block, block requires exactly 3)\");\n\n  // === \"Alike\" components: same type required ===\n  it.todo(\"should charge 75 G base premium for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block, different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 120 G base premium for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // === Modifier scope on multi-item policies ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to cursed item base premium, not policy total: cursed sword (100 G) + plain amulet (60 G) → 160 G + 50 G curse = 210 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: cursed items (50% surcharge) ===\n  it.todo(\"should add 50% cursed surcharge: cursed sword → 100 G base + 50 G cursed = 150 G + 5 G fee = 155 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: high enchantment (≥5, 30% surcharge) ===\n  it.todo(\"should add 30% high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment >= 5: sword with enchantment 5 → 100 G base + 30 G = 130 G + 5 G fee = 135 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not add high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment 4: sword → 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: loyalty discount (≥2 years, 20%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO\");\n\n  // === Modifier: first insurance surcharge (10%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 10% first insurance surcharge for new customer (0 years with MHPCO)\");\n\n  // === Modifier: follow-up contract discount (15%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 15% follow-up contract discount after first quote\");\n\n  // === Integration: Newcomer with a cursed sword ===\n  it.todo(\"should calculate premium 165 G for newcomer (0 years) with cursed sword (enchantment 3): 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 + 5 fee = 165\");\n\n  // === Integration: Long-standing customer's second contract ===\n  it.todo(\"should calculate premium 160 G for 3-year customer, second contract, cursed sword (enchantment 7): 100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchant - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155 + 5 fee = 160\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage event ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item: dragon attack damages sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G) → payout 600 G\");\n\n  // === Claim: Standard reimbursement (no special clauses) ===\n  it.todo(\"should pay 400 G for regular steel sword (enchantment 3) damaged 500 G: 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay 100 G for rune damage 200 G: 200 - 100 deductible = 100\");\n\n  // === Claim: High enchantment ≥8 → 50% reimbursement ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse 50% for enchantment >= 8: steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon material → full reimbursement ===\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material sword enchantment 5, damage 800 G → 800 - 100 deductible = 700\");\n\n  // === Claim: Enchantment ≥8 AND dragon material → 50% rule wins ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 50% rule when both enchantment >= 8 and dragon material: dragon sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage event (explicit) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damage event (not per claim): verifying from spec example\");\n\n  // === Policy cap ===\n  it.todo(\"should have cap of 2x insurance sum: sword + amulet → sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value: cursed sword → cap 2000\");\n  it.todo(\"should not affect insurance sum with block discount: sword + 3 runes block → sum 1750, cap 3500\");\n\n  // === Cap exhaustion ===\n  it.todo(\"should exhaust cap across successive claims: sword (sum 1000, cap 2000), first 1500 claim → payout 1400, cap remaining 600; second 1500 claim → payout 600, cap remaining 0\");\n\n  // === Multiple items of same type ===\n  it.todo(\"should allow two swords in policy → insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"should treat multiple damage entries of same type separately\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim when damages contain more entries of a type than insured\");\n\n  // === Rounding ===\n  it.todo(\"should round premium up in favor of MHPCO: 197.5 G → 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round payout down in MHPCO's favor: 350.5 G → 350 G\");\n\n  // === CLI I/O format: Schema example ===\n  it.todo(\"should process schema example: customer 5 years, quote amulet silver enchantment 2, claim damage 200 → premium and payout\");\n\n  // === Scenario: sequential steps ===\n  it.todo(\"should process multiple sequential quote and claim steps in a scenario\");\n});"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1377,"output":1787,"cacheRead":11264,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14428,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949736630,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-08a144fd-e02a-4582-8bd1-696e9ce5fcf0","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_423ab9c4bd144a469b8dca09","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 5724 bytes to /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949742912},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office — quote and claim operations\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 35\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple → complex):\n1. Empty item list → premium 5 G (only processing fee)\n2. Quote with unknown item type → error (broomstick)\n3. Claim with damage to item not in policy → error\n4. Claim with negative damage amount → error\n5. Base premium: sword → 100 G\n6. Base premium: amulet → 60 G\n7. Base premium: staff → 80 G\n8. Base premium: potion → 40 G\n9. Base premium: single rune → 25 G\n10. Base premium: single moonstone → 25 G\n11. 2 runes → 50 G base premium (no block)\n12. 3 runes → 60 G base premium (block applies)\n13. 4 runes → 100 G base premium (no block)\n14. 7 runes → 175 G base premium (no block)\n15. 2 runes + 1 moonstone → 75 G (different types, no block)\n16. 3 runes + 3 moonstones → 120 G (two separate blocks)\n17. Cursed surcharge scoped to cursed item: cursed sword + plain amulet → 210 G\n18. Cursed surcharge: cursed sword → 155 G\n19. High enchantment surcharge (≥5): enchantment 5 sword → 135 G\n20. No high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment 4 sword → 105 G\n21. Loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years\n22. First insurance surcharge (10%)\n23. Follow-up contract discount (15%)\n24. Newcomer with cursed sword → 165 G\n25. 3-year customer, second contract, cursed sword enchantment 7 → 160 G\n26. Deductible per damaged item: sword 500 + amulet 300 → payout 600 G\n27. Standard reimbursement: steel sword enchantment 3, damage 500 → 400 G\n28. Rune damage 200 G → payout 100 G\n29. Enchantment ≥8: steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 → 400 G\n30. Dragon material: dragon sword enchantment 5, damage 800 → 700 G\n31. Both enchantment ≥8 and dragon material: 50% rule wins → 400 G\n32. Deductible applies per damage event\n33. Cap: sword + amulet → sum 1600, cap 3200\n34. Cursed sword cap based on unmodified insurance value → cap 2000\n35. Block discount does not affect insurance sum: sword + 3 runes → sum 1750, cap 3500\n36. Cap exhaustion across successive claims\n37. Two swords in policy → sum 2000, cap 4000\n38. Multiple damage entries of same type treated separately\n39. Reject claim when damages exceed insured count of a type\n40. Round premium up: 197.5 → 198\n41. Round payout down: 350.5 → 350\n42. Schema example: quote + claim\n43. Multiple sequential steps\n\n**Next Step**: Invoke `red` skill to activate the first test.\n\nNow let me start the Red phase for test 1. But first, I need to create the implementation stub file so there's something to import"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_146790cf1de64188a4639fec","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"// Claim Office implementation stub\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): unknown => {\n  return undefined as unknown;\n};","path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2214,"output":898,"cacheRead":12288,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15400,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949742913,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bd56d963-dd7f-4a7c-9b3b-5d806c772772","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_146790cf1de64188a4639fec","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 131 bytes to /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949749818},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me read the red SKILL.md once more (already read above) and then activate test 1.\n\n## Red -- Test 1: Empty item list → premium 5 G\n\n**Step 1: Activate the test.** I'll convert the first `it.todo` to an