ure developers can immediately understand what `5` represents without reading test descriptions\n\n**Mass Change**: 3 → 3 (unchanged — swapped one constant for one binding)\n\n**Analysis**: Mass stayed the same because we replaced an inline constant (magic number `5`) with a named binding (`PROCESSING_FEE_G`). While mass didn't decrease, clarity improved significantly — the constant name now reveals the intent of the value, which is where it originally was an opaque \"5.\" This is a textbook case of Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumping APP: we maintained the same mass but dramatically improved readability.\n\n**Tests**: All 1 passing, 42 todo — all green."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 1\nRecent Green phase: Hardcoded return `{ results: [{ premium: 5 }] }` for empty item list producing 5 G premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 1\nRecent Green phase: Hardcoded return `{ results: [{ premium: 5 }] }` for empty item list producing 5 G premium.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784949768655},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the code before ref"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_22d88716ce9d4a089c0b2b91","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4ee6ca7da8504c039d2adc00