Added explicit TypeScript type aliases (`Item`, `Step`, `Scenario`) to replace the deeply nested inline types in the cast, improving readability.\n- **Mass reduction**: 108 → 90 (16.7% lower), primarily from removing the duplicate loop over `scope.steps`.\n\nBenefits:\n- One pass over steps instead of two (eliminating the duplicate `for (const step of scenario.steps)` loop and the duplicate `step.op === \"quote\"` check)\n- Single point of truth for policy tracking — item validation and policy building are unified\n- Clearer function name that reveals both responsibilities\n- Explicit types make intent clearer\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Report Completion\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Merged `validateItemTypes` and `validateClaimDamages` into `buildPoliciesAndValidateItems` — single-pass validation that eliminates duplicate iteration over steps\n**Mass Change**: 108 → 90 (-18, -16.7%)\n**Tests**: All 3 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 3\nRecent Green phase: Added `validateClaimDamages` function — tracks policy item types from quote steps and throws error when claim damage references an item not in the policy.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 3\nRecent Green phase: Added `validateClaimDamages` function — tracks policy item types from quote steps and throws error when claim damage references an item not in the policy.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.