ages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 100 }] } }\n      ]\n    })).toThrow();\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should exit with error for claim with damage entry having negative amount\");\n\n  // === Item values and base premiums ===\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a sword: 100 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for an amulet: 60 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a staff: 80 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a potion: 40 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a single rune (component): 25 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a single moonstone (component): 25 G\");\n\n  // === Building block of 3 alike components ===\n  it.todo(\"should charge 50 G base premium for 2 runes (no block)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 60 G base premium for 3 runes (block applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 100 G base premium for 4 runes (no block, block requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 175 G base premium for 7 runes (no block, block requires exactly 3)\");\n\n  // === \"Alike\" components: same type required ===\n  it.todo(\"should charge 75 G base premium for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block, different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 120 G base premium for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // === Modifier scope on multi-item policies ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to cursed item base premium, not policy total: cursed sword (100 G) + plain amulet (60 G) → 160 G + 50 G curse = 210 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: cursed items (50% surcharge) ===\n  it.todo(\"should add 50% cursed surcharge: cursed sword → 100 G base + 50 G cursed = 150 G + 5 G fee = 155 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: high enchantment (≥5, 30% surcharge) ===\n  it.todo(\"should add 30% high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment >= 5: sword with enchantment 5 → 100 G base + 30 G = 130 G + 5 G fee = 135 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not add high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment 4: sword → 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: loyalty discount (≥2 years, 20%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO\");\n\n  // === Modifier: first insurance surcharge (10%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 10% first insurance surcharge for new customer (0 years with MHPCO)\");\n\n  // === Modifier: follow-up contract discount (15%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 15% follow-up contract discount after first quote\");\n\n  // === Integration: Newcomer with a cursed sword ===\n  it.todo(\"should calculate premium 165 G for newcomer (0 years) with cursed sword (enchantment 3): 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 + 5 fee = 165\");\n\n  // === Integration: Long-standing customer's second contract ===\n  it.todo(\"should calculate premium 160 G for 3-year customer, second contract, cursed sword (enchantment 7): 100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchant - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155 + 5 fee = 160\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage event ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item: dragon attack damages sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G) → payout 600 G\");\n\n  // === Claim: Standard reimbursement (no special clauses) ===\n  it.todo(\"should pay 400 G for regular steel sword (enchantment 3) damaged 500 G: 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay 100 G for rune damage 200 G: 200 - 100 deductible = 100\");\n\n  // === Claim: High enchantment ≥8 → 50% reimbursement ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse 50% for enchantment >= 8: steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon material → full reimbursement ===\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material sword enchantment 5, damage 800 G → 800 - 100 deductible = 700\");\n\n  // === Claim: Enchantment ≥8 AND dragon material → 50% rule wins ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 50% rule when both enchantment >= 8 and dragon material: dragon sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage event (explicit) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damage event (not per claim): verifying from spec example\");\n\n  // === Policy cap ===\n  it.todo(\"should have cap of 2x insurance sum: sword + amulet → sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value: cursed sword → cap 2000\");\n  it.todo(\"should not affect insurance sum with block discount: sword + 3 runes block → sum 1750, cap 3500\");\n\n  // === Cap exhaustion ===\n  it.todo(\"should exhaust cap across successive claims: sword (sum 1000, cap 2000), first 1500 claim → payout 1400, cap remaining 600; second 1500 claim → payout 600, cap remaining 0\");\n\n  // === Multiple items of same type ===\n  it.todo(\"should allow two swords in policy → insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"should treat multiple damage entries of same type separately\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim when damages contain more entries of a type than insured\");\n\n  // === Rounding ===\n  it.todo(\"should round premium up in favor of MHPCO: 197.5 G → 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round payout down in MHPCO's favor: 350.5 G → 350 G\");\n\n  // === CLI I/O format: Schema example ===\n  it.todo(\"should process schema example: customer 5 years, quote amulet silver enchantment 2, claim damage 200 → premium and payout\");\n\n  // === Scenario: sequential steps ===\n  it.todo(\"should process multiple sequential quote and claim steps in a scenario\");\n});"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949835457},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c26c1588726f485585d0fc3e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE_G = 5;\n\nconst KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\"sword\", \"amulet\", \"staff\", \"potion\", \"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst validateItemTypes = (scenario: { steps: Array<{ op: string; items?: Array<{ type: string }> }> }): void => {\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\" && step.items) {\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst validateClaimDamages = (scenario: { steps: Array<{ op: string; items?: Array<{ type: string }>; policy?: number; incident?: { damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }> } }> }): void => {\n  const policies: Array<Set<string>> = [];\n  \n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\" && step.items) {\n      const itemTypes = new Set(step.items.map(i => i.type));\n      policies.push(itemTypes);\n    }\n    if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policyIdx = step.policy!;\n      const policyItems = policies[policyIdx];\n      if (!policyItems) {\n        throw new Error(`Invalid policy index: ${policyIdx}`);\n      }\n      if (step.incident) {\n        for (const damage of step.incident.damages) {\n          if (!policyItems.has(damage.itemType)) {\n            throw new Error(`Item ${damage.itemType} not in policy`);\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): unknown => {\n  const scenario = input as { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }, steps: Array<{ op: string; items?: Array<{ type: string }>; policy?: number; incident?: Array<{ damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }> }> }> };\n  validateItemTypes(scenario);\n  validateClaimDamages(scenario);\n  return { results: [{ premium: PROCESSING_FEE_G }] };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949835457},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me run the tests to confirm all"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5a6b190fe60149d5a8764a8f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>