ect literal constant (1)\n\nTabulated:\n| Category | Old processScenario | New processScenario |\n|----------|---------------------|---------------------|\n| Constants | 6 | 5 |\n| Bindings | 7 | 4 |\n| Invocations | 14 | 14 |\n| Conditionals | 3 | 3 |\n| Loops | 2 | 1 (`map` = 5) |\n| Assignments | 0 | 0 |\n\nNew mass for `processScenario`: 5c + 4b + 14×2i + 3×4cond + 1×5loop = 5 + 4 + 28 + 12 + 5 = **54**\n\nOld mass for `processScenario`: 6c + 7b + 14×2i + 3×4cond + 2×5loop = 6 + 7 + 28 + 12 + 10 = **63**\n\n---\n\nFull file mass before/after:\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|--------|-------|\n| File-level | 19c + 4b + 2i = 29 | unchanged: 29 |\n| `processSteps` | 124 | unchanged: 124 |\n| `calculateQuotePremium` | 25 | unchanged: 25 |\n| `processScenario` | 63 | **54** |\n| **Total** | **241** | **232** |\n\nMass delta: **-9** (reduction)\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n\n1. **Replaced `for` loop + mutable array with `.map()`** in `processScenario`: Eliminated the mutable `results` array, the `push` calls, and the explicit loop. The `.map()` concisely expresses \"transform each step into a result.\"\n\n2. **Removed unused binding `policies`**: The return value of `processSteps` was assigned to `policies` but never read. Dropped the binding entirely since `processSteps` is only called for side-effect validation.\n\n3. **Inlined `items` variable**: The `const items = step.items ?? [];` intermediate variable was unnecessary — the expression fits inline in the `calculateQuotePremium` call.\n\n**Benefits**:\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: The `.map()` pattern clearly expresses \"this is a transformation,\" which is more idiomatic in functional-style TypeScript.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewer Elements)**: Reduced 3 bindings and 1 loop (total mass -9).\n- **No duplication introduced**: `processSteps` remains the single source of truth for validation.\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Report Completion\n\n**Refactoring**: Replaced mutable `for`-loop + push pattern with `.map()`, removed unused bindings\n**Mass Change**: 241 → 232 (delta: -9)\n**Tests**: All 5 passing ✅\n\nRefactoring Complete."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added `BASE_PREMIUMS` lookup table and `calculateQuotePremium` function. `processScenario` now iterates over steps and builds results array properly (quote → premium, claim → placeholder).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added `BASE_PREMIUMS` lookup table and `calculateQuotePremium` function. `processScenario` now iterates over steps and builds results array properly (quote → premium, claim → placeholder).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784949913651},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the codebase, then apply the refactoring rules"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3c53166710774db59c5e641e","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_83217035308a40c2974c32d6","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":239,"output":107,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6490,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949913673,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8cce92d8-3976-46be-a89f-9bcac99ae87c","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3c53166710774db59c5e641e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE_G = 5;\n\nconst KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\"sword\", \"amulet\", \"staff\", \"potion\", \"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ntype Item = { type: string };\ntype Step = { op: string; items?: Item[]; policy?: number; incident?: { damages: Array<{ itemType: string; amount: number }> } };\ntype Scenario = { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }; steps: Step[] };\n\nconst processSteps = (steps: Step[]): Array<Set<string>> => {\n  const policies: Array<Set<string>> = [];\n\n  for (const step of steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      const itemTypes = new Set<string>();\n      for (const item of items) {\n        if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n          throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n        }\n        itemTypes.add(item.type);\n      }\n      policies.push(itemTypes);\n    }\n    if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policyIdx = step.policy!;\n      const policyItems = policies[policyIdx];\n      if (!policyItems) {\n        throw new Error(`Invalid policy index: ${policyIdx}`);\n      }\n      if (step.incident) {\n        for (const damage of step.incident.damages) {\n          if (damage.amount < 0) {\n            throw new Error(`Negative damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n          }\n          if (!policyItems.has(damage.itemType)) {\n            throw new Error(`Item ${damage.itemType} not in policy`);\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return policies;\n};\n\nconst calculateQuotePremium = (items: Array<{ type: string }>): number => {\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    basePremium += BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n  }\n  return basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE_G;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): unknown => {\n  const scenario = input as Scenario;\n  const policies = processSteps(scenario.steps);\n  \n  const results: Array<{ premium?: number; payout?: number; remainingCap?: number }> = [];\n  \n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      results.push({ premium: calculateQuotePremium(items) });\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      results.push({});\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949914858},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_83217035308a40c2974c32d6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office\", () => {\n  // === Edge Cases ===\n  it(\"should return premium 5 G for empty item list (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }]\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should exit with error for quote with unknown item type (e.g. broomstick)\", () => {\n    expect(() => processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"broomstick\" }] }]\n    })).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"should exit with error for claim with damage to item not in policy\", () => {\n    expect(() => processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 100 }] } }\n      ]\n    })).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"should exit with error for claim with damage entry having negative amount\", () => {\n    expect(() => processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: -200 }] } }\n      ]\n    })).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  // === Item values and base premiums ===\n  it(\"should calculate base premium for a sword: 100 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }]\n    }) as { results: Array<{ premium?: number }> };\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(100 + 5); // base 100 + 5 processing fee\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for an amulet: 60 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a staff: 80 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a potion: 40 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a single rune (component): 25 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should calculate base premium for a single moonstone (component): 25 G\");\n\n  // === Building block of 3 alike components ===\n  it.todo(\"should charge 50 G base premium for 2 runes (no block)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 60 G base premium for 3 runes (block applies)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 100 G base premium for 4 runes (no block, block requires exactly 3)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 175 G base premium for 7 runes (no block, block requires exactly 3)\");\n\n  // === \"Alike\" components: same type required ===\n  it.todo(\"should charge 75 G base premium for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (no block, different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"should charge 120 G base premium for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // === Modifier scope on multi-item policies ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to cursed item base premium, not policy total: cursed sword (100 G) + plain amulet (60 G) → 160 G + 50 G curse = 210 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: cursed items (50% surcharge) ===\n  it.todo(\"should add 50% cursed surcharge: cursed sword → 100 G base + 50 G cursed = 150 G + 5 G fee = 155 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: high enchantment (≥5, 30% surcharge) ===\n  it.todo(\"should add 30% high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment >= 5: sword with enchantment 5 → 100 G base + 30 G = 130 G + 5 G fee = 135 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should not add high-enchantment surcharge for enchantment 4: sword → 100 G base + 5 G fee = 105 G\");\n\n  // === Modifier: loyalty discount (≥2 years, 20%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO\");\n\n  // === Modifier: first insurance surcharge (10%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 10% first insurance surcharge for new customer (0 years with MHPCO)\");\n\n  // === Modifier: follow-up contract discount (15%) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 15% follow-up contract discount after first quote\");\n\n  // === Integration: Newcomer with a cursed sword ===\n  it.todo(\"should calculate premium 165 G for newcomer (0 years) with cursed sword (enchantment 3): 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 + 5 fee = 165\");\n\n  // === Integration: Long-standing customer's second contract ===\n  it.todo(\"should calculate premium 160 G for 3-year customer, second contract, cursed sword (enchantment 7): 100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchant - 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance - 15 follow-up = 155 + 5 fee = 160\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage event ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damaged item: dragon attack damages sword (500 G) and amulet (300 G) → payout 600 G\");\n\n  // === Claim: Standard reimbursement (no special clauses) ===\n  it.todo(\"should pay 400 G for regular steel sword (enchantment 3) damaged 500 G: 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay 100 G for rune damage 200 G: 200 - 100 deductible = 100\");\n\n  // === Claim: High enchantment ≥8 → 50% reimbursement ===\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse 50% for enchantment >= 8: steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n\n  // === Claim: Dragon material → full reimbursement ===\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material sword enchantment 5, damage 800 G → 800 - 100 deductible = 700\");\n\n  // === Claim: Enchantment ≥8 AND dragon material → 50% rule wins ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 50% rule when both enchantment >= 8 and dragon material: dragon sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → 500 - 100 deductible = 400\");\n\n  // === Claim: Deductible per damage event (explicit) ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damage event (not per claim): verifying from spec example\");\n\n  // === Policy cap ===\n  it.todo(\"should have cap of 2x insurance sum: sword + amulet → sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value: cursed sword → cap 2000\");\n  it.todo(\"should not affect insurance sum with block discount: sword + 3 runes block → sum 1750, cap 3500\");\n\n  // === Cap exhaustion ===\n  it.todo(\"should exhaust cap across successive claims: sword (sum 1000, cap 2000), first 1500 claim → payout 1400, cap remaining 600; second 1500 claim → payout 600, cap remaining 0\");\n\n  // === Multiple items of same type ===\n  it.todo(\"should allow two swords in policy → insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"should treat multiple damage entries of same type separately\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim when damages contain more entries of a type than insured\");\n\n  // === Rounding ===\n  it.todo(\"should round premium up in favor of MHPCO: 197.5 G → 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round payout down in MHPCO's favor: 350.5 G → 350 G\");\n\n  // === CLI I/O format: Schema example ===\n  it.todo(\"should process schema example: customer 5 years, quote amulet silver enchantment 2, claim damage 200 → premium and payout\");\n\n  // === Scenario: sequential steps ===\n  it.todo(\"should process multiple sequential quote and claim steps in a scenario\");\n});"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949914858},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me run the tests to confirm current state:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_18151f3a08a449a3938d180d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2711,"output":128,"cacheRead":6400,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":9239,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949914859,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-dd2718f6-18d2-4b11-9875-a3f6c7e57acd","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_18151f3a08a449a3938d180d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-22-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (43 tests | 38 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  5 passed | 38 todo (43)\n   Start at  03:25:16\n   Duration  154ms (transform 26ms, setup 0ms, collect 26ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949916307},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 5 tests pass. Now let me systematically apply the refactoring rules.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\n\nLet me evaluate each function and key variable:\n\n**`processScenario`**: Takes a scenario (with customer and steps) and returns results. Name is accurate —